  "observations": "The original comparison begun before context compaction is reused within this same independent gate. All three current width previews inspected individually. Five isotherms retain three increasingly short subcritical plateaus, a bold critical isotherm with K, an upper nonplateau isotherm, dashed two-sided coexistence envelope, and source pressure/volume guides. Corrected horizontal volume order is V1, V1-prime, V_c, V2-prime, V2, explicitly distinguished from reversed source endpoint families by page97 errata and passed SCI. Tiered labels retain their horizontal anchors. English critical c notation is declared modernization, not source lettering. No extra highest-plateau guides, numeric scales, extrapolated branches, or cultural labels.",
